A||||7||kevin||speaker location||||1||
Z||000000||kevin||06-08-2000||03:09 PM||||I have a 85 SE with speakers in the seats. I thought it would be neat to add quality speakers in the quarter panel location like the 86,87, and 88's. Will 4x6's or any other size fit? Remember, I need and will get high end speakers. Any thoughts? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||06-08-2000||03:23 PM||||I dont see why not. 4x6's go in the sail panels. I changed my speakers out on two of my 86's...not that big of an ordeal. Ive never delt w/models with speakers in the headrests though. I would have to think that right off the top of my head, you could replace the inside sail panels with those w/ speaker cutouts, or cut them out yourself, then wire em up. Stereo/speaker installation is really quite an easy process. You will need to get 2 new clips for the inner sail panels though, they tend to break when you pull them out. Most parts stores carry them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-08-2000||05:55 PM||||<B>MUCH</B> more involved than that.  I had planned on doing the same thing, but decided against it once I found out what it would take.  1st, the '86-'88s had a hole cut out of the metal behind the sail panel for the speaker.  The '84s and '85 don't.  This is the major stumbling block.  Also, the '86-'88s had a plastic mounting ring around the speakers.  I suppose you could do without this, but if you decide to undertake this project, you might as well do it right.  Here's a better choice, IMHO.  Try some 5 1/4" separates.  With very little modification, the mids will fit in the stock dash openings and the tweeters can go behind the the small, lower portion of the side vents.  If you feel like you absolutely must do the '86-'88 rear speakers, LMK as I have all of the parts needed to change your car over.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||06-08-2000||09:13 PM||||I have seen an 85 GT with 6.5" coax in the side panels. As Monkey said, it would be some work, but it can be done. Probably would need something without much depth, like MB Quart. <P>Monkey, do you still have your Pioneer 4x10's? would you consider selling them seperate from the 4x6's?||||reg||1
Z||000004||mbramble||06-08-2000||10:48 PM||||I just replaced the sail speakers in my 87 Coupe a couple days ago and I'm not sure you could get speakers into those holes without those plastic mounting rings.  In the speaker holes, there is some sort of an obstruction between the inner/outer metal frame toward the front of the holes.  The plastic mounting rings are not flat, they allow the front of the speaker to be mounted further out of the hole to miss that obstruction -- they act as spacers because you can't fit the speaker magnets into those holes.  I bought some decent 3-way 4x6 speakers that had good sized magnets (at least twice size of stock speakers and I had a heck of a time getting them mounted.  Finally did though but had to remove the sound deadening insulation that was in the speaker hole.  Even the stock speaker magnets are a pretty tight fit in those holes and I dont think they would fit without the plastic ring that acts as a spacer to clear the obstructions.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mbramble||06-08-2000||10:54 PM||||I also just replaced the dash speakers with a mid range and tweeter on each side.  Made a thin plywood 'adapter' the size of the original speaker frame and mounted the 4" round mid and 1" tweeter to this adapter.  Sounds great -- can't tell it when the covers are in place.  But, anything would have sounded better than my original 4x10's.  The 'diaphram' (or whatever the tech term is) that connects the cone to the frame was completely gone on both speakers.  The top edge of the cones was just hanging there.....||||reg||1
Z||000006||phillip||06-09-2000||02:19 AM||||do '85s have 3rd brake lights? i have one 4" rear speaker in my '87 that is in a pod that is part of my third brake light. it points toward the window and gets a mixed mono signal.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||06-09-2000||10:39 AM||||Not from the factory.  I've got one in mine, though.  Just need to wire it up.  Anyone remember the thread about that?  I need some info (i.e. what wires go where and something about about the ts not working right?).||||reg||1
